<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai Housing IPO to trade Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Hyundai Housing IPO to trade Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean Hyundai Housing and Industrial Development Co's initial public offering (IPO) will begin trading on Wednesday along with three other initial offerings, the Korea Stock Exchange said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Hyundai Housing, a unit of the Hyundai Group, will list 6.2 million new shares. The stock was offered at a price of 14,000 won per share.</p>
<p>Dong Yang Elevator Co's 600,000 new shares will also begin trading on Wednesday. They were initially offered at 22,000 won each.  </p>
<p>Transistor maker AUK Corp's 500,000 new shares. had been offered at 15,000 won.</p>
<p>Korea Electronic Terminal Co's 280,000 new shares had been offered at 36,000 won per share.</p>
<p>All four offerings were made on September 5-6</p>
